# Force the Apple App Site Association file to be served as JSON. It has no file
# extension, so Cloudflare can't infer the type; iOS/validators expect
# application/json. (assetlinks.json already gets application/json from its
# extension, but we pin it too for clarity.)
# Cloudflare Workers Assets defaults these files to `Cache-Control: public,
# max-age=0, must-revalidate`. The Android App Links verifier and Google's
# Digital Asset Links cache behave poorly with a no-cache statement file — a
# clean Play-Store install can fail to auto-verify (domain stuck in state
# 1024) even though the file content + fingerprints are correct. Serve both
# association files with a normal, cacheable policy instead.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/.well-known/assetlinks.json
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
